@lang en
IMPORT prelude
IMPORT daydate
IMPORT `nii-il33-nouns`
IMPORT `nii-il33-readings`
IMPORT `nii-schedule-a1-ages`
IMPORT `nii-s2a-residence`

-- ===========================================================================
-- National Insurance Law: who is insured under Chapters 5, 6, 7 (s 158), 8, 9, 10 and 11. Row IL-33.
-- The statuses s 335 reads ("מבוטח לפי פרק ה׳" and so on), derived from the facts of the person on a day
-- instead of taken as inputs (capstone GAPS.md item 9, row IL-08's s335 module).
--
-- Each rule answers "is the person insured under this Chapter on the day". Evaluation is left to right
-- and stops at the first condition that decides (FALSE AND x is FALSE, TRUE OR x is TRUE), so a person a
-- cheap condition excludes is answered even where a later condition would be declined.
--
-- Source lines: s 75-76 (943-957); s 150 (1403-1405); s 158 (1441-1454); s 6B (289-290);
-- ss 180-181 (1818-1830); s 195 (1921-1942); s 223 (2165-2178); ss 240, 243 (2438-2449).
-- ===========================================================================

§ `Insured persons, Chapter by Chapter`

§§ `The common conditions: an adult, below the retirement age`

-- "שמלאו לו 18 שנים": has completed 18 years, i.e. 216 months (s 150, s 158(1), s 195, s 240(a)).
@ref NII s 150, s 195, s 240(a), s 158(1): "שמלאו לו 18 שנים"
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`an adult: the person` p `has completed 18 years on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
    `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` 216 `on` `the day` `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)

§§ `Chapter 5 (ss 75-76)`

-- src:944 | (א) אלה המבוטחים לפי פרק זה:
-- src:945 | (1) עובד, למעט שוטר כמשמעותו בחוק המשטרה, סוהר כמשמעותו בחוק שירות בתי הסוהר ועובד שירותי הבטחון כמשמעותו בסעיף 63א לחוק שירות המדינה;
-- src:946 | (2) עובד עצמאי, למעט מי שנמנה עם סוג אנשים שהוצאו מכלל עובדים עצמאיים, לענין סעיף זה, בתקנות ולאחר התייעצות עם ועדת העבודה והרווחה;
-- src:956 | (א) העובד בחוץ לארץ מבוטח לפי פרק זה אם הוא ומעבידו הם תושבי ישראל וחוזה העבודה נקשר בישראל, או אף אם חוזה העבודה לא נקשר בישראל ובמקום העבודה אין ביטוח נפגעי עבודה חובה לפי החוק ונמסרה הודעה על קיומו של החוזה כפי שנקבע בתקנות.
-- src:957 | (ב) על אף הוראות סעיף קטן (א), אם שהה העובד בחוץ לארץ, תקופה העולה על חמש שנים רצופות, לא יהיה מבוטח לפי פרק זה אם לא התיר השר או מי שהשר הסמיך לכך את ביטוחו בתקופת עבודתו בחוץ לארץ שלאחר חמש השנים.
-- s 76(a): a worker abroad is insured if he and his employer are residents of Israel and the contract was
-- made in Israel, "or even if" it was not made in Israel and at the workplace there is no compulsory
-- work-injury insurance and notice of the contract was given as the regulations prescribe. The "even if"
-- dispenses with one condition (the place the contract was made); the residence of both stays (fork C4,
-- class (b): the other grammatical reading insures two foreign parties on a foreign contract under this
-- Law). s 76(b): after more than five consecutive years abroad, not insured unless permitted.
@ref NII s 76, lines 956-957
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 76 — a worker abroad is insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        NOT (    (p's work)'s `has stayed abroad for more than five consecutive years`
             AND NOT (p's work)'s `the Minister or his delegate permitted the insurance after the five years`)
    AND (p's work)'s `the employer is an Israeli resident`
    AND (   (p's work)'s `the contract of employment was made in Israel`
         OR (    (p's work)'s `no compulsory work injury insurance applies at the place of work`
             AND (p's work)'s `notice of the contract of employment was given as the regulations prescribe`))
    AND `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`)

@ref NII s 75(a)(1), s 76, lines 945, 956-957
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75(a)(1) — an employee insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        (p's work)'s `an employee`
    AND NOT (p's work)'s `a police officer, a prison officer or a security-service employee`
    AND (   NOT (p's work)'s `works outside Israel`
         OR `s 76 — a worker abroad is insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd)

-- (2): a self-employed person, except a class the regulations exclude. Abroad: fork C3.
@ref NII s 75(a)(2), line 946; fork C3
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75(a)(2) — a self-employed person insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        (p's work)'s `a self-employed person`
    AND NOT (p's work)'s `of a class of self-employed persons the regulations exclude`
    AND (   NOT (p's work)'s `works outside Israel`
         OR CONSIDER (rd's `a self-employed person who works outside Israel`)
            WHEN `insured wherever the work is done`                  THEN TRUE
            WHEN `insured only if the work is done in Israel`         THEN FALSE
            WHEN `declined where the two readings differ`             THEN
                REFUSE "section 75(a)(2) insures a self-employed person and does not say whether that reaches work done outside Israel; section 76, which limits insurance abroad, speaks only of an employee")

@ref NII s 75(a)(3) to (8), lines 947-952
GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75(a)(3) to (8) — in a further category insured under Chapter 5:` p MEANS
    count ((p's work)'s `further categories insured under section 75(a)`) GREATER THAN 0

@ref NII s 75(a), lines 944-952
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 75 — insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 75(a)(1) — an employee insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    OR  `s 75(a)(3) to (8) — in a further category insured under Chapter 5:` p
    OR  `s 75(a)(2) — a self-employed person insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd

§§ `Chapters 6 and 9 (ss 150 and 195): a resident of 18, below the retirement age`

-- src:1405 | ”מבוטח“ – תושב ישראל שמלאו לו 18 שנים, וטרם הגיע לגיל פרישה;
-- src:1929 | ”מבוטח“ – תושב ישראל שמלאו לו 18 שנים וטרם הגיע לגיל הפרישה;
@ref NII s 150 "מבוטח", line 1405
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 150 — insured under Chapter 6:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`)
    AND `an adult: the person` p `has completed 18 years on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    AND NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd

@ref NII s 195 "מבוטח", line 1929
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 195 — insured under Chapter 9:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`)
    AND `an adult: the person` p `has completed 18 years on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    AND NOT `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd

§§ `Chapter 7 (s 158) and s 6B`

-- src:1444 | (1) תושב ישראל או תושב ארעי שמלאו לו 18 שנים וטרם הגיע לגיל הקבוע לגביו, בהתאם לחודש לידתו, בחלק ב׳ בלוח א׳1, והוא עובד הזכאי לשכר שמעבידו חייב בתשלום דמי ביטוח בעדו;
-- src:289 | סעיף 6ב – מבוטח שהוא בעל שליטה בחברת מעטים [תיקון: תשס״ג־8]
-- src:290 | הוראות פרקים ז׳ ו־ח׳ לא יחולו על בעל שליטה בחברת מעטים.
-- s 158 "מבוטח" (1): a resident or a temporary resident of 18 or over who has not reached the Part B age
-- of his month of birth, "and he is a worker entitled to wages for which his employer must pay insurance
-- contributions". s 158 "עובד" leaves out a member of a collective or renewed kibbutz regarded as a worker
-- under s 3 or 3A(a). "Temporary resident" (תושב ארעי) is not defined in the Law (fork R2): the case says
-- whether the person is one. The controlling shareholder is left out by s 6B, not by s 158; this rule
-- leaves him in (row IL-08's s 335(e) leaves him out itself) and `s 6B` below says he is out.
@ref NII s 158 "מבוטח" (1), line 1444; "עובד", line 1453
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 158 — insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        (p's work)'s `an employee`
    AND NOT (p's work)'s `a member of a collective or renewed kibbutz regarded as a worker under section 3 or 3A(a)`
    AND (p's work)'s `entitled to wages on which the employer must pay insurance contributions`
    AND `an adult: the person` p `has completed 18 years on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    AND (   (p's residence)'s `a temporary resident`
         OR `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`))
    AND NOT `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` (`Schedule A1, Part B — the maximum age in months for unemployment insurance of a person born on` (p's `date of birth`)) `on` `the day` `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)

-- (2): a soldier who served regular service under the Security Service Law, other than service under a
-- career commitment, from the day of release and for one year from that day.
@ref NII s 158 "מבוטח" (2), line 1445
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 158 — insured under paragraph (2), a soldier released from regular service:` p `on` `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `released from regular service`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST released THEN
            `the day` AT LEAST released
        AND `the day` LESS THAN `add years` released 1

-- (3): a volunteer in national service or community volunteering (the temporary provision adds a person
-- serving in civil-national service) for one year from the end of the service, if the service lasted
-- long enough. Two texts (fork C1). The temporary provision says 24 months and applies to one who
-- began his service before 31 August 2026. The permanent text measures the service against the period a
-- female conscript serves under s 16(1) of the Security Service Law, which is not deposited, so a
-- service begun on or after that day is refused by name. The proviso: a woman who served at least six
-- months and married within 30 days of stopping is deemed to have served the full period, and the year
-- counts from the day she stopped.
@ref NII s 158 "מבוטח" (3), lines 1446-1447; fork C1
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 158 — insured under paragraph (3), a completed national or community service:` p `on` `the day` MEANS
    CONSIDER p's `completed national or community service`
    WHEN NOTHING THEN FALSE
    WHEN JUST s THEN
            `the day` AT LEAST s's `the day the service ended`
        AND `the day` LESS THAN `add years` (s's `the day the service ended`) 1
        AND (   s's `a woman who served at least six months and married within 30 days of the day she stopped`
             OR IF   s's `the service began before 31 August 2026`
                THEN s's `the months served` AT LEAST 24
                ELSE REFUSE "section 158 \"insured\" (3), in its permanent text, measures the service against the period a female conscript serves under section 16(1) of the Security Service Law, and that Law is not deposited: needs a source")

@ref NII s 158 "מבוטח" (1) to (3)
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 158 — insured under paragraph (1), (2) or (3) of the definition of insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 158 — insured under paragraph (1) of the definition of insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    OR  `s 158 — insured under paragraph (2), a soldier released from regular service:` p `on` `the day`
    OR  `s 158 — insured under paragraph (3), a completed national or community service:` p `on` `the day`

-- s 6B: "הוראות פרקים ז׳ ו־ח׳ לא יחולו על בעל שליטה בחברת מעטים".
@ref NII s 6B, lines 289-290
GIVEN p IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 6B — Chapters 7 and 8 do not apply to the person:` p MEANS
    (p's work)'s `a controlling shareholder in a closely-held company`

@ref NII s 6B, s 158
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 158 and s 6B — insured under Chapter 7:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        NOT `s 6B — Chapters 7 and 8 do not apply to the person:` p
    AND `s 158 — insured under paragraph (1), (2) or (3) of the definition of insured:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd

§§ `Chapter 8 (ss 180-181)`

-- src:1820 | ”עובד“ – מי שמבוטח או היה מבוטח כעובד לפי פרק ה׳;
-- src:1830 | המבוטחים לפי פרק זה הם עובד וקופת גמל.
-- s 181: the insured are "עובד" (a worker) and a provident fund. s 180 "עובד": one who is or was insured as
-- an employee under Chapter 5. s 6B takes a controlling shareholder out. A provident fund is not a person
-- of this model.
@ref NII s 180 "עובד", s 181, s 6B, lines 1820, 1830, 289-290
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 180-181 — a worker insured under Chapter 8:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        NOT `s 6B — Chapters 7 and 8 do not apply to the person:` p
    AND (   (p's work)'s `was insured as an employee under Chapter 5 at some earlier time`
         OR `s 75(a)(1) — an employee insured under Chapter 5:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd)

§§ `Chapter 11 (ss 240 and 243)`

-- src:2439 | (א) בכפוף להוראות סעיף קטן (ב), תושב ישראל שמלאו לו 18 שנים מבוטח לפי פרק זה, להוציא מי שביום שבו נעשה לראשונה תושב ישראל כבר הגיע לגיל הקבוע לגביו, בהתאם לחודש לידתו, בחלק ג׳ בלוח א׳1, ולגבי אישה – אם ביום שבו נעשתה לראשונה תושבת ישראל כבר הגיעה לגיל הפרישה.
-- src:2449 | השר רשאי לקבוע סוגי בני אדם שעל אף הוראות סעיף 240 לא יהיו מבוטחים לפי פרק זה; ואולם המוסד רשאי, אם נתבקש לעשות כן, לבטח אדם מאלה או להפסיק ביטוחו לפי תנאים שנקבעו.
-- s 240(a): a resident of 18 or over is insured, except one who, on the day he first became a resident,
-- had already reached the age Part C of Schedule A1 fixes for him by his month of birth, and, for a woman,
-- one who on the day she first became a resident had already reached the retirement age. s 243: the
-- Minister may fix classes who are not insured despite s 240; the Institute may insure one of them on
-- request (the regulations are not deposited: fork C2, an input).
@ref NII s 240(a), line 2439; Schedule A1 Part C
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 240(a) — already past the age on first becoming a resident:` p `, reading` rd MEANS
    CONSIDER ((p's residence)'s `the day the person first became an Israeli resident`)
    WHEN NOTHING THEN
        REFUSE "section 240(a) turns on the day the person first became an Israeli resident, and the case does not give it (a person resident from birth has the day of birth)"
    WHEN JUST first THEN
        CONSIDER p's sex
        WHEN `female` THEN
            `s 1 — the retirement age is reached by` p `on` first `, reading` rd
        WHEN `male` THEN
            `a person born on` (p's `date of birth`) `has reached the age in months` (`Schedule A1, Part C — the age in months, for a person who is not a woman, at which he is not insured under Chapter 11, born on` (p's `date of birth`)) `on` first `, reading` (rd's `the day an age is reached`)

@ref NII s 240(a), s 243, lines 2439, 2449
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 240 — insured under Chapter 11:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`)
    AND `an adult: the person` p `has completed 18 years on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    AND (   NOT ((p's `Chapter 11`)'s `of a class the Minister has excluded from insurance under section 243`)
         OR (p's `Chapter 11`)'s `insured at the person's own request under the regulations under section 243`)
    AND NOT `s 240(a) — already past the age on first becoming a resident:` p `, reading` rd

§§ `Chapter 10, long-term care (s 223)`

-- src:2175 | (1) מבוטח לפי פרק י״א;
-- src:2178 | (4) תושב ישראל שעלה לפי חוק השבות, או תושב ישראל שבידו אשרה ורישיון לישיבת קבע או אשרה ורישיון לישיבת ארעי מסוג א/5, לפי חוק הכניסה לישראל, שניתן לו סל קליטה מהמשרד לקליטת העליה, והכל אם אינם מבוטחים בביטוח אזרחים ותיקים וביטוח שאירים;
@ref NII s 223 "מבוטח" (1), (4), lines 2175, 2178
GIVEN p         IS A `A person for the statuses of the Law`
      `the day` IS A DATE
      rd        IS A `The readings this row takes where the text does not decide`
GIVETH A BOOLEAN
`s 223 — insured for long-term care:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd MEANS
        `s 240 — insured under Chapter 11:` p `on` `the day` `, reading` rd
    OR  (    (   (p's absorption)'s `immigrated under the Law of Return`
              OR (p's absorption)'s `holds a permanent-residence visa and licence, or an A/5 temporary visa and licence`)
         AND (p's absorption)'s `was given an absorption basket by the Ministry of Aliyah and Integration`
         AND `s 2A — an Israeli resident:` p `on` `the day` `, reading 183 as` (rd's `exactly 183 days in section 2A`))
